<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
  <PropertyGroup>
    <PackageId>KhaozEngine.SegmentRig</PackageId>
    <Version>$(KhaozEngineVersion)</Version>
    <Description>Render-free pose core for rigid-segment characters, the visual counterpart of KhaozEngine.Locomotion. A body is a set of rigid pieces posed every frame by procedural code rather than by a skinned animation clip, so this package answers with transforms and angles and draws nothing at all: BodyPose (world metres plus a yaw), BodyRig and QuadrupedRig proportions and joint frames, the distance-driven WalkCycle and its WalkPose channel contract, the IdleBreath rest cycle, the four-beat QuadrupedGait, and the action strokes over those same channels (AttackTrajectory's shared clock, AttackSwing, SlashSwing, ChopSwing, ProcessingSwing, BlockRaise and the four-legged Headbutt), then the HumanoidSkeleton and QuadrupedSkeleton composers that turn a rig plus a pose into one world transform per piece, and SegmentSockets for what a hand holds. Time is seconds or a normalized phase, a cadence is always a caller-supplied float of seconds, and there is no tick count anywhere, so one cycle serves a slow fixed-tick game and a fast continuous one alike. Depends on nothing: not Render3D, not TileWorld, not Netcode, not Gpu, not Primitives. In the Foundation umbrella.</Description>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
